      "solution": "my $tokens;\nmy @inputs;\nmy @carts;\n\nchomp(my $n = <STDIN>);\nchomp($tokens=<STDIN>);\n@inputs = split(/ /,$tokens);\nfor my $carts (@inputs) {\n    push(@carts,$carts);\n}\nchomp(my $actions = <STDIN>);\n\nfor my $action (split(//,$actions)) {\n    if($action eq \"T\") {\n        my $max=0;\n        my $maxi;\n        for my $i (0..$#carts) {\n           ($max,$maxi)=($carts[$i],$i) if($carts[$i]>$max);\n        }\n        if($max==0) {\n            print \"IMPOSSIBLE\\n\";\n            exit;\n        }\n        $carts[$maxi]--;\n    } else {\n        my $min=1000;\n        my $mini;\n        for my $i (reverse(0..$#carts)) {\n           ($min,$mini)=($carts[$i],$i) if($carts[$i]<$min);\n        }\n        $carts[$mini]++;\n    }\n}\n\nprint join(\" \",@carts).\"\\n\";",
      "statement": "A grocery store has [[n]] lines of available shopping carts next to each other. Each line is indexed from 1 to [[n]]. Line [[i]] has [[carts_i]] shopping carts. To balance out the lines, there are specific rules regarding how customers must take and return shopping carts. Shopping carts are taken and returned one at a time by customers.\n\nTaking a shopping cart requires taking it from the line with the largest number of shopping carts. If there are multiple such lines, it must be taken from the line with the smallest index.\n\nReturning a shopping cart requires returning it to the shortest line of shopping carts. If there are multiple shortest lines, return the shopping cart to the one with the largest index.\n\nGiven [[n]], the initial number of shopping carts [[carts_i]] in each shopping cart line and a string [[actions]] containing a sequence of action characters ({{T}} for take, {{R}} for return), output the resulting number of shopping carts [[carts_i]] in each shopping cart line after all actions have been performed from left to right. If at any time, a shopping cart shall be taken when none are left, output {{IMPOSSIBLE}} instead.\n\nBecause the simulation can start from any initial condition, it is allowed to return a cart that hasn't been taken before.",
